<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en-US"><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/rss</id><title>Unreal Engine - News, Developer Interviews, Spotlights, Tech Blogs</title><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/rss" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><description>Feed containing the latest news, developer interviews, events, spotlights, and tech blogs related to Unreal.  Unreal Engine 4 is a professional suite of tools and technologies used for building high-quality games and applications across a range of platforms. Unreal Engine 4’s rendering architecture enables developers to achieve stunning visuals and also scale elegantly to lower-end systems.</description><language>en-US</language><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;Check out the top Fortnite islands from the UEFN Student Bootcamp&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmufwe9sf1e4807n238yg532r</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmufwe9sf1e4807n238yg532r&quot; /&gt; The UEFN Student Bootcamp has wrapped! Watch this sizzle reel of some of the best Fortnite islands created during this intensive three-week course, which was completed by over 300 students.</content><category>Games</category><category>Learning</category><category>UEFN</category><category>Fortnite</category><category>UEFN Student Bootcamp</category><published>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/learning/check-out-the-top-fortnite-islands-from-the-uefn-student-bootcamp" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/learning/check-out-the-top-fortnite-islands-from-the-uefn-student-bootcamp</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SILENT HILL: Townfall&lt;/em&gt; delivers haunting psychological horror at its very best with UE5&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmupvlpy417fc06o4w3ilrrrv</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmupvlpy417fc06o4w3ilrrrv&quot; /&gt; Discover how UE5 tools including Lumen, Nanite, and MetaHuman helped Screen Burn Interactive craft complex, beautifully rendered scenes and compelling characters for chilling, slow-burn survival horror &lt;em&gt;SILENT HILL: Townfall&lt;/em&gt;.</content><category>Games</category><category>RealityScan</category><category>Blueprints</category><category>Sequencer</category><category>Unreal Insights</category><category>MetaHuman</category><category>Nanite</category><category>Lumen</category><category>UE5</category><category>Screen Burn Interactive</category><category>SILENT HILL: Townfall</category><category>Interviews</category><published>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/silent-hill-townfall-delivers-haunting-psychological-horror-at-its-very-best-with-ue5" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/silent-hill-townfall-delivers-haunting-psychological-horror-at-its-very-best-with-ue5</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;UEFN Professional Bootcamp: Prepare for Unreal Engine 6&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmv8881ms1tgv06ogxws7dypa</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmv8881ms1tgv06ogxws7dypa&quot; /&gt; With Epic’s roadmap bringing together Unreal Engine and UEFN in UE6, build your UEFN skills with our free UEFN Professional Bootcamp for games industry pros. Register today to create and publish a playable Fortnite island and strengthen your portfolio.</content><category>Games</category><category>Verse</category><category>Fortnite</category><category>Unreal Editor for Fortnite</category><category>UE6</category><category>UEFN Professional Bootcamp</category><category>Learning</category><published>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/news/uefn-professional-bootcamp-prepare-for-unreal-engine-6" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/news/uefn-professional-bootcamp-prepare-for-unreal-engine-6</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;Fuse Games uses UE5 to make a fast and authentic &lt;em&gt;Star Wars&lt;/em&gt;™ racing game&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmuwzh49t20io06n5bq8q34o6</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmuwzh49t20io06n5bq8q34o6&quot; /&gt; &lt;em&gt;Star Wars: &lt;/em&gt;Galactic Racer™ blends high-speed racing with a roguelite twist. Discover how Fuse Games used Unreal Engine 5’s Lumen, Nanite, and World Partition to create striking visuals that do justice to the game’s innovative gameplay and worldbuilding.</content><category>Games</category><category>Lumen</category><category>Nanite</category><category>World Partition</category><category>Unreal Insights</category><category>PCG</category><category>UE5</category><category>Fuse Games</category><category>Star Wars: Galactic Racer</category><category>Interviews</category><published>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/fuse-games-uses-ue5-to-make-a-fast-and-authentic-star-wars-racing-game" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/fuse-games-uses-ue5-to-make-a-fast-and-authentic-star-wars-racing-game</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Gears of War: E-Day&lt;/em&gt; sees a return to dark, survival-horror roots with UE5&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmubohz9w0ub807ojp8e9wd7h</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmubohz9w0ub807ojp8e9wd7h&quot; /&gt; With the latest major main-series installment of &lt;em&gt;Gears of War&lt;/em&gt; about to drop, we caught up with The Coalition to find out how UE5 helped recapture the desperate “destroyed beauty” aesthetic of the original games—while evolving gameplay, animation, and more.</content><category>Games</category><category>Lumen</category><category>Nanite</category><category>World Partition</category><category>Gameplay Abilities System</category><category>MegaLights</category><category>Sequencer</category><category>The Coalition</category><category>Gears of War: E-Day</category><category>Third Person Shooter</category><category>Interviews</category><published>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/gears-of-war-e-day-sees-a-return-to-dark-survival-horror-roots-with-ue5" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/gears-of-war-e-day-sees-a-return-to-dark-survival-horror-roots-with-ue5</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;September’s Epic learning content: MetaHumans, physics, animation, and more&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmuejuiik0tpc07n2hdrv1sgy</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmuejuiik0tpc07n2hdrv1sgy&quot; /&gt; Check out this month’s free learning resources, including an exploration of the MetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture plugin, a journey into UE 5.8’s MCP server, a look at the new Experimental AnimGen workflow—and much more.</content><category>Games</category><category>Film &amp; Television</category><category>Animation</category><category>Unreal Engine 5.8</category><category>Chaos</category><category>AI</category><category>Mocap</category><category>MetaHuman</category><category>Nanite</category><category>AnimGen plugin</category><category>Learning</category><published>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/learning/septembers-epic-learning-content-metahumans-physics-animation-and-more" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/learning/septembers-epic-learning-content-metahumans-physics-animation-and-more</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;TT Games brings Gotham City to life in LEGO &lt;em&gt;Batman:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;Legacy of the Dark Knight&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmtsu7vy06vlx07ogtmlfxbf1</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmtsu7vy06vlx07ogtmlfxbf1&quot; /&gt; We caught up with TT Games to find out how UE5 features such as World Partition, the Gameplay Ability System, and more helped them fulfill their vision for an open world Gotham City in LEGO &lt;em&gt;Batman:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;Legacy of the Dark Knight&lt;/em&gt;.</content><category>Games</category><category>Open World</category><category>World Partition</category><category>Gameplay Abilities System</category><category>Sequencer</category><category>UE5</category><category>Unreal Insights</category><category>LEGO Batman: Legacy of the Dark Knight</category><category>TT Games</category><category>Interviews</category><published>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/tt-games-brings-gotham-city-to-life-in-lego-batman-legacy-of-the-dark-knight" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/developer-interviews/tt-games-brings-gotham-city-to-life-in-lego-batman-legacy-of-the-dark-knight</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;Unreal Engine 5.8 is now available&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmqgp745a38sh07og8o13mphx</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmqgp745a38sh07og8o13mphx&quot; /&gt; Build bigger, better, more differentiated worlds in less time; easily populate them with high-fidelity animated characters and custom vegetation; and light and render them at the speed and quality your audiences demand.</content><category>Games</category><category>Mobile</category><category>Indies</category><category>Film &amp; Television</category><category>Architecture</category><category>Automotive &amp; Transportation</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Animation</category><category>Broadcast &amp; Live Events</category><category>Virtual Production</category><category>Lumen</category><category>MegaLights</category><category>UE 5.8</category><category>News</category><published>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/news/unreal-engine-5-8-is-now-available" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/news/unreal-engine-5-8-is-now-available</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;The road to Unreal Engine 6&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmq9rgre02go607lp7of937we</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmq9rgre02go607lp7of937we&quot; /&gt; We have started the road to UE6, where Unreal Engine and UEFN will come together into a single, unified engine. Read more about our vision, transition plans, and timeline.</content><category>Games</category><category>Mobile</category><category>Indies</category><category>Film &amp; Television</category><category>Animation</category><category>UE 6</category><category>News</category><published>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/news/the-road-to-ue-6" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/news/the-road-to-ue-6</id></entry><entry><title>&lt;p&gt;State of Unreal 2026: Top news from the show&lt;/p&gt;</title><icon>https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmqi2n8o673uc07n72ce9l2xy</icon><content type="html">&lt;img src=&quot;https://cms-assets.unrealengine.com/AiKUh5PQCTaOFnmJDZJBfz/cmqi2n8o673uc07n72ce9l2xy&quot; /&gt; At State of Unreal 2026, we shared our vision for Unreal Engine 6, released Unreal Engine 5.8, open-sourced the next-generation version control system Lore, highlighted UEFN’s growing developer ecosystem, and previewed improvements to the Epic Games Store. Learn more here.</content><category>Games</category><category>Film &amp; Television</category><category>Architecture</category><category>Automotive &amp; Transportation</category><category>Broadcast &amp; Live Events</category><category>Simulation</category><category>UEFN</category><category>Indies</category><category>Mobile</category><category>Unreal Fest Chicago 2026</category><category>Lore</category><category>UE 5.8</category><category>UE 6</category><category>State of Unreal 2026</category><category>Events</category><published>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</published><updated>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</updated><link href="https://www.unrealengine.com/news/state-of-unreal-2026-top-news-from-the-show" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link><id>https://www.unrealengine.com/news/state-of-unreal-2026-top-news-from-the-show</id></entry></feed><script>(function(){function c(){var b=a.contentDocument||(a.contentWindow&&a.contentWindow.document);if(b){var d=b.createElement('script');d.innerHTML="window.__CF$cv$params={r:'a4ea5b0cc8dadc4d',t:'MTc5MjY5MTU0NQ=='};var a=document.createElement('script');a.src='/cdn-cgi/challenge-platform/scripts/jsd/main.